## 3. Sub-Pixel Halton Jitter & Motion Vector Rules

- **Halton `(2, 3)` Sequence Length:** Scale phase count by the upscaling ratio:
  $$N_{\text{phases}} = \text{round}\left(8 \cdot \left(\frac{W_{\text{display}}}{W_{\text{render}}}\right)^2\right)$$
  (e.g., `8` phases at Native DLAA, `18` at Quality `1.5x`, `32` at Performance `2.0x`).
- **History Reset (`InReset = 1`):** Always assert `RequestHistoryReset()` on camera cuts, level loads, save loads, and binocular/scope zoom transitions.

## Windows 10/11 & Cross-Platform Parity (`windows-linux-cross-os-runtime-bridge`)
- On Linux (Wine/Proton + DXVK-NVAPI), verify `/usr/lib/nvidia/wine/_nvngx.dll` and `nvngx_dlss.dll` (`310.7.0+`) are exposed with `PROTON_ENABLE_NVAPI=1 DXVK_ENABLE_NVAPI=1`.

